ll  has two dragons John's probably going to  become a dragon rider as well and we'll  talk more about that in the second thing  that I think was really important but  the first thing was Tyrians little  speech to Daenerys about a line of  succession now it's long been debated  that since the  and throwing probably isn't going to be  important in the end that there may be a  shift where a different kind of  government is put in place and most of  those theories revolve around Tyrians  input in that process so when he brought  that up in the episode it's a pretty big  deal the points he makes are valid she  goes into battle and she could die at  any time and as he pointed out as she  said she isn't able to have children he  says that the Nights Watch has a way of  choosing a successor and so does the  Ironborn despite their many flaws so  he's talking about an election more or  less maybe not exactly how we do it  nowadays in most of the civilized world  but it's a pretty interesting thought  considering what this story is about you  think about the big picture the stories  about all the squabbling and craziness  and insanity that people go through for  this power to sit on the throne and  that's what leads a lot of people to  look at it more as a unimportant ending  to the book Daenerys is talking about  breaking the wheel is in contradiction  with a regular line of secession in that  she would have an heir and then her heir  would rule and it would keep going like  that for as long as they were able to  stay there the idea that Tyrion is  putting out there is for apps people  will decide and that truly will make the  world a better place which in the  context of everything else is more of a  sensible way for things to end up now of  course no one makes it on the Iron  Throne  for a couple reasons but in the end I  think this is something to think about  how do they go from here to where they  end up how do they get this society to  let go of the idea that your name is  everything and your family history is  everything we'll just have to see how  that goes  now the second really big crazy thing  and these two things are probably more  interesting to me because they were  never spoiled by leaks because no one  knew about them  the second big thing was absolutely when  John kills the white Walker and the  other one the other whites who are bound  to it immediately fall that was a big  surprise because like I said no one had  known that prior to this episode airing  and it's pretty big in the sense that if  you kill the night king you have to  imagine that that's going to pretty much  decimate the entire army of the Dead now  there's a lot of thought about how that  all works and up until this was revealed  in the show my thought was that fire  whites and everything else aside the ice  whites the ones we've known since the  very beginning they were basically all  connected together so the night King  raised them or they were raised by that  magic and they all sort of functioned as  one big organism with a very simple  purpose like that's the most practical  way that I could think of you know like  he can't think for all of them so they  don't think they just do one thing and  they do it well and they're bound to a  hive mind or a collection if you will  when we saw this happen in the one sense  that would undermine everything like you  just have to kill one guy and then the  army falls what I think we should all  keep in mind though and Ford is is that  that means that this guy must be much  much harder to kill than just walking up  there and stabbing him now of course  people will go quickly into the comments  and post it has to be with Lightbringer  Azula as the temperature steel to create  Lightbringer yeah I mean that's one  possible scenario that that is a literal  prophecy that will come true exactly how  it is but it is like a thing because  this is going to end up shaping how they  attack and approach this war throughout 